arden, herbal garden, arid garden, and landscaped areas showcasing tropical and indigenous Philippine plant species. The site also includes a small zoological section, making it an educational and recreational destination for families, students, and nature enthusiasts.";s:12:"entrance_fee";d:20.01;s:21:"classification_status";s:9:"POTENTIAL";}i:4;a:11:{s:2:"id";i:97;s:4:"name";s:13:"Ma-Cho Temple";s:8:"category";s:28:"Historical,Cultural Heritage";s:5:"image";s:48:"/api/serve-image.php?file=spot_6a5713b70034d.jpg";s:8:"latitude";d:16.623102;s:9:"longitude";d:120.317585;s:6:"rating";d:3;s:6:"visits";i:0;s:11:"description";s:450:"Ma-Cho Temple is the first Taoist temple in the Philippines and is dedicated to the Chinese sea goddess Mazu (Ma-Cho). Built in 1975 on a hill approximately 70 feet above sea level, the one-hectare temple overlooks the West Philippine Sea and features the Majestic Five-Door Gate, Bell Tower, Drum Tower, bamboo garden, and traditional Chinese architecture. It is a popular destination for prayer, cultural appreciation, sightseeing, and photography.";s:12:"entrance_fee";d:0;s:21:"classification_status";s:5:"EXIST";}i:5;a:11:{s:2:"id";i:100;s:4:"name";s:11:"Sanfernando";s:8:"category";s:19:"Mountain,Waterfalls";s:5:"image";s:48:"/api/serve-image.php?file=spot_6a5734f5a6ad0.jpg";s:8:"latitude";d:16.61584;s:9:"longitude";d:120.31765;s:6:"rating";d:5;s:6:"visits";i:0;s:11:"description";s:12:"this is demo";s:12:"entrance_fee";d:20;s:21:"classification_status";s:6:"EMERGE";}}